What:		/dev/mt6797-speech
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	Gemini Linux maintainers
Description:
		Root-only MT6797 MD1 speech-control record transport, independent
		of the ALSA PCM sample interface. One open file owner at a time.
		Each read returns exactly one complete CCCI speech record, at
		most 3456 bytes. An undersized buffer returns EMSGSIZE without
		consuming the record. Records are never concatenated or split.

		The 16-byte little-endian header comprises data0, data1,
		channel/sequence, reserved. Mailboxes have data0=FFFFFFFF and
		data1=(message-ID<<16)|parameter. Data records carry the total
		byte count in data1 and message-ID/parameter in reserved.
		RX channel is 4; TX channel is 5. The driver assigns TX sequence
		and channel and checks actual HS2 readiness before admission.

		TX supports AP mailbox IDs 2f00..2fff and in-band dynamic speech
		parameters 2f79 with the stock six-byte a2a2/type19/length prefix.
		All payload bytes must be supplied by the real board/call owner;
		there are no default calibration bytes or startup responses.

		After a stock-listed ACK command, subsequent ordinary commands
		wait for its real matching RX acknowledgement. The only exceptions
		are exact mailbox replies 2f75/parameter0/reserved0 and
		2f90/parameter0/reserved0. Each requires one credit granted by a
		successful read of the corresponding valid AF75/AF90 request by
		the current owner. AF75 is a mailbox with a u16 network parameter;
		AF90 is a data record with parameter194, exactly194 payload bytes
		and little-endian magic1234 at payload offset0. RF policy and codec
		string handling remain userspace responsibilities.

		Requests are bounded to32 outstanding, including queued/unread,
		copied and in-flight replies. EFAULT/EMSGSIZE grants no credit and
		preserves the record. A reply without credit fails EPERM; malformed
		reply parameters fail EPROTO. An unpublished TX error restores its
		credit, except after terminal reset/detach. Replies never clear the
		pending command ID or change speech-active state. POLLOUT can
		therefore report a writable credited reply while an ordinary
		command is still blocked by its ACK; callers must dispatch pending
		requests rather than retry unrelated commands on that readiness.

		A successful write
		reports submission, not modem completion. The call owner must use
		poll and a bounded completion deadline; the kernel sends no fake
		ACK, timeout retry or automatic speech-off. Closing with a pending
		command, active speech engine or unanswered request (even unread)
		makes the endpoint terminal until
		native modem reset, preventing stale ACK reuse by a subsequent owner.
		An idle reset purges earlier queued records. A reset racing a read
		or an outstanding request fences the endpoint and clears credits.
		Malformed RX, overflow, reset during a transaction and unmatched
		ACKs also make this endpoint terminal. Cellular AT/data remain
		independent.

		Fatal/remove/shutdown wakes readers/writers and polls ERR/HUP.
		An open file pins a terminal object after parent removal; no
		parent callback remains reachable once detach finishes.
